Here is the complete, step-by-step procedure to run **Programs 44, 45, 47, and 48** from scratch in your Linux terminal. 

*(Note: Your screenshot had 44, 45, 47, and 48. I will cover those exact 4 programs).*

### 🛠️ Step 0: Setup & Cleanup
First, stop any running Tomcat server by pressing `Ctrl+C` in the terminal where it's running. Then, run these commands to create the correct folder structure and download the MySQL driver (needed for 47 & 48):

```bash
# Go to your home directory
cd ~

# Create the correct folder structure
mkdir -p MyApp/WEB-INF/classes
mkdir -p MyApp/WEB-INF/lib

# Download the MySQL JDBC Driver directly into your app
wget -P MyApp/WEB-INF/lib https://repo1.maven.org/maven2/com/mysql/mysql-connector-j/8.3.0/mysql-connector-j-8.3.0.jar
```

---

### 📝 Step 1: Create all 4 Java Files
Copy and paste this entire block into your terminal. It will generate all 4 files inside `~/MyApp`.

```bash
cd ~/MyApp

# -----------------------------------------
# 44: Simple Servlet
cat << 'EOF' > P44.java
import jakarta.servlet.annotation.WebServlet;
import jakarta.servlet.http.*;
import java.io.*;
@WebServlet("/p44")
public class P44 extends HttpServlet {
    protected void doGet(HttpServletRequest q, HttpServletResponse r) throws IOException {
        r.getWriter().print("<h2>Program 44: Simple Servlet Works!</h2>");
    }
}
EOF

# -----------------------------------------
# 45: Session Tracking
cat << 'EOF' > P45.java
import jakarta.servlet.annotation.WebServlet;
import jakarta.servlet.http.*;
import java.io.*;
@WebServlet("/p45")
public class P45 extends HttpServlet {
    protected void doGet(HttpServletRequest q, HttpServletResponse r) throws IOException {
        HttpSession s = q.getSession();
        Integer c = (Integer) s.getAttribute("visits");
        c = (c == null) ? 1 : c + 1;
        s.setAttribute("visits", c);
        r.getWriter().print("<h2>Program 45: Visit Count = " + c + "</h2><p>Refresh to increase!</p>");
    }
}
EOF

# -----------------------------------------
# 47: JDBC Database Access (Read from authors table)
# NOTE: Change "root", "root" to your actual MySQL username/password
cat << 'EOF' > P47.java
import jakarta.servlet.annotation.WebServlet;
import jakarta.servlet.http.*;
import java.io.*;
import java.sql.*;
@WebServlet("/p47")
public class P47 extends HttpServlet {
    protected void doGet(HttpServletRequest q, HttpServletResponse r) throws IOException {
        try (var c = DriverManager.getConnection("jdbc:mysql://localhost/cse1", "root", "root");
             var rs = c.createStatement().executeQuery("SELECT * FROM authors")) {
            r.getWriter().print("<h2>Program 47: Database Data</h2>");
            while (rs.next()) r.getWriter().print(rs.getInt("id") + " - " + rs.getString("name") + " - " + rs.getString("email") + "<br>");
        } catch (Exception e) {
            r.getWriter().print("<h2>DB Error:</h2> " + e.getMessage());
        }
    }
}
EOF

# -----------------------------------------
# 48: Full Web App (DB + Session)
cat << 'EOF' > P48.java
import jakarta.servlet.annotation.WebServlet;
import jakarta.servlet.http.*;
import java.io.*;
import java.sql.*;
@WebServlet("/p48")
public class P48 extends HttpServlet {
    protected void doGet(HttpServletRequest q, HttpServletResponse r) throws IOException {
        r.getWriter().print("<h2>Program 48: Full Web App</h2>");
        // 1. Session Tracking
        HttpSession s = q.getSession();
        Integer c = (Integer) s.getAttribute("hits");
        c = (c == null) ? 1 : c + 1;
        s.setAttribute("hits", c);
        r.getWriter().print("Session Hits: " + c + "<br><br>");
        
        // 2. Database Access
        try (var conn = DriverManager.getConnection("jdbc:mysql://localhost/cse1", "root", "root");
             var rs = conn.createStatement().executeQuery("SELECT name FROM authors LIMIT 1")) {
            if (rs.next()) r.getWriter().print("DB Connected. First Author: " + rs.getString("name"));
        } catch (Exception e) {
            r.getWriter().print("DB Error: " + e.getMessage());
        }
    }
}
EOF
```

---

### ⚙️ Step 2: Compile and Deploy
Run these commands to compile the Java files and copy the app to Tomcat:

```bash
cd ~/MyApp
# Compile all Java files
javac -cp ~/apache-tomcat-10.1.34/lib/servlet-api.jar -d WEB-INF/classes *.java

# Deploy the app to Tomcat
cp -r ~/MyApp ~/apache-tomcat-10.1.34/webapps/
```

---

### 🚀 Step 3: Start Tomcat
Start the server:
```bash
~/apache-tomcat-10.1.34/bin/catalina.sh run
```

*(Wait a few seconds until you see "Server startup in [XXXX] milliseconds" in the terminal).*

---

### 🌐 Step 4: Test in Browser
Open your browser and test the following URLs:

1. **Program 44:** `http://localhost:8080/MyApp/p44`
   * *What you'll see:* "Program 44: Simple Servlet Works!"
2. **Program 45:** `http://localhost:8080/MyApp/p45`
   * *What you'll see:* "Visit Count = 1". Refresh the page. It will say "Visit Count = 2".
3. **Program 47:** `http://localhost:8080/MyApp/p47`
   * *What you'll see:* Data from your `authors` table. *(If you get an error, it means MySQL isn't running or your username/password is different).*
4. **Program 48:** `http://localhost:8080/MyApp/p48`
   * *What you'll see:* Both the session hit count and the database author name on the same page.

*(To stop the server, press `Ctrl+C` in your terminal).*

